# Kanaku — environment configuration map
#
# There is intentionally NO root .env. Each workspace owns its environment:
#
#   backend/.env          all backend secrets & tuning (DB, JWT, SendGrid,
#                         AI provider keys, rate limits, workers)
#                         → template: backend/.env.example
#
#   backend/.env.test     DEDICATED test database for the jest suite
#                         (never production, never a shared schema)
#                         → template: backend/.env.test.example
#
#   frontend/.env         VITE_* variables only (compiled into the bundle —
#                         never put secrets here; anything VITE_ is public)
#                         → template: frontend/.env.example
#
# Production values live in the platform dashboards, not in files:
#   Render (backend)  — render.yaml lists every required key (sync: false)
#   Vercel (frontend) — project Environment Variables
#
# Quick start:
#   cp backend/.env.example backend/.env       # fill in DB + JWT at minimum
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#   npm run setup && npm run dev
